      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A computerized method of acquiring and analyzing rest and exercise test 12-lead electrocardiographic and three-dimensional lead vectorcardiographic data before and after cardiac rehabilitations is described. Fourteen coronary heart disease patients were exercise tested before and after a mean of five months of aerobic exercise training, The only significant ST-segment improvements were found in three-dimensional space. Spatial measurements should be considered in the assessment of electrocardiographic changes secondary to exercise training."},
